==Battleground==
*10 [[Shakurel Doge]]s spawn, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*2 [[Shakurel Gory|Shakurel Gories]] spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Shakurel Face]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Shakurel Tiger (Enemy)|Shakurel Tigers]] spawn, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
**5 [[Shakurel Tiger (Enemy)|Shakurel Tigers]] spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**7 [[Shakurel Lion (Enemy)|Shakurel Lions]] spawn, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
**4 [[Shakurel Panda (Enemy)|Shakurel Pandas]] spawn, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Because of the buffs on all the enemies here. You will need strong [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|area attackers]] like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] and/or [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]], just to name a few. [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] helps greatly in defeating Shakurel Face quickly, as well as [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] just for general damage. [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]]-wise, any [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]] Uber like [[Shadow Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Shadow Gao]] or [[Relentless Gladios (Uber Rare Cat)|Relentless Gladios]] will do well, as well as any [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] Uber that can kill Shakurel Face quickly, such as [[Saber (Uber Rare Cat)|Saber]] or [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Warlock and Pierre]]. Strong generalists also help here.

